From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] qasf: Negotiate and deliver compressed ASF streams.

The Witch's Love Diary explicitly connects the ASF reader to WMA and WMV
decoder DMOs. Offering only decoded PCM/RGB makes the first connection fail
with VFW_E_CANNOT_CONNECT, which the application retries indefinitely.

Cache the original stream media types from IWMProfile and advertise them
after the existing decoded formats. Select compressed sample delivery only
when the downstream connection negotiates that format, size its allocator
using GetMaxStreamSampleSize, and forward OnStreamSample to the existing
sample delivery path using the actual stream number.

Keep decoded formats preferred for existing automatic graphs. No decoder
passthrough or application-specific connection workaround is needed.

Add coverage for media type enumeration, connections to the WMA/WMV DMO
wrappers, and delivery of compressed audio and video samples.

References:
https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/755
https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/wmformat/to-deliver-compressed-samples-with-the-asynchronous-reader

---
